1
00:01:51,077 --> 00:01:52,877
You won't get away with this!

2
00:01:52,877 --> 00:01:54,777
That looks like the Frankie family.

3
00:01:54,777 --> 00:01:57,777
Hey, those are our bags! How'd they get them?

4
00:01:57,777 --> 00:01:59,577
Money! My money!

5
00:02:01,777 --> 00:02:05,277
Galley Law Company, a grand site, dock number one!

6
00:02:08,477 --> 00:02:10,377
Hold it right there, Pauly!

7
00:02:11,077 --> 00:02:13,077
You're not getting away this time!

8
00:02:13,077 --> 00:02:14,877
I'm telling you, I'll get you the money!

9
00:02:14,877 --> 00:02:16,577
You just have to wait a little longer!

10
00:02:17,077 --> 00:02:17,877
Is that...?

11
00:02:17,877 --> 00:02:19,077
Yes, it's Pauly.

12
00:02:19,077 --> 00:02:21,577
The debt collectors are after him again.

13
00:02:21,577 --> 00:02:23,577
Ugh! Where are you going with our money?

14
00:02:23,577 --> 00:02:27,077
That would be real nice if you're lending us 200 million berries like that!

15
00:02:27,077 --> 00:02:29,577
Bunch of cowards! I'm gonna make you pay!

16
00:02:29,577 --> 00:02:31,577
Why'd you give our money to those guys?

17
00:02:31,577 --> 00:02:34,577
What do you take me for? I didn't give those jerks anything! They stole it!

18
00:02:34,577 --> 00:02:35,577
What?

19
00:02:35,577 --> 00:02:37,577
Give us the money!

20
00:02:37,577 --> 00:02:40,577
For the last time, I can't give you money if I don't have it!

21
00:02:40,577 --> 00:02:43,577
Stop making excuses and pay up!

22
00:02:43,577 --> 00:02:46,577
You're gonna chase me all the way to my grave, aren't you?

23
00:02:46,577 --> 00:02:49,077
Jaggera's been just in time, too!

24
00:02:49,077 --> 00:02:50,077
Hyah!

25
00:02:51,077 --> 00:02:52,077
Rope!

26
00:02:52,077 --> 00:02:53,077
Action!

27
00:02:57,077 --> 00:02:59,577
Hey, that's one of the ship rides from Galley Law, ain't it?

28
00:02:59,577 --> 00:03:02,577
Sorry, fellas, but I gotta borrow those Jaggera's now!

29
00:03:02,577 --> 00:03:04,077
Time for my round turn!

30
00:03:04,077 --> 00:03:06,077
hinaus behaviour

31
00:03:13,577 --> 00:03:15,077
Ha ha ha ha ha!

32
00:03:15,077 --> 00:03:17,077
Waaaah!

33
00:03:17,077 --> 00:03:19,577
Ugh...

34
00:03:19,577 --> 00:03:20,577
Ha ha ha.

35
00:03:20,577 --> 00:03:21,577
Ugh!

36
00:03:21,577 --> 00:03:22,577
Ugh!

37
00:03:24,577 --> 00:03:25,577
Ugh!

38
00:03:25,577 --> 00:03:26,577
Ugh!

39
00:03:26,577 --> 00:03:27,577
Ugh!

40
00:03:27,577 --> 00:03:28,577
Ugh!

41
00:03:28,577 --> 00:03:29,577
You punk!

42
00:03:29,577 --> 00:03:30,577
Just wait!

43
00:03:30,577 --> 00:03:31,577
We'll get you next time!

44
00:03:31,577 --> 00:03:32,577
So long, gentlemen.

45
00:03:32,577 --> 00:03:34,577
It was a wonderful race, as always.

46
00:03:34,577 --> 00:03:36,577
Take care, and maybe you can try again next week!

47
00:03:36,577 --> 00:03:37,577
Goddammit.

48
00:03:37,577 --> 00:03:38,577
Ugh!

49
00:03:38,577 --> 00:03:44,577
I gotta admit, for a Jagera, you sure have a good sense of dramatic timing.

50
00:03:44,577 --> 00:03:45,577
Hmm.

51
00:03:48,577 --> 00:03:49,577
That was close.

52
00:03:49,577 --> 00:03:52,577
Those shipwrights of yours have got some pretty fancy moves.

53
00:03:52,577 --> 00:03:53,577
That they do.

54
00:03:53,577 --> 00:03:54,577
Hey, buddy!

55
00:03:54,577 --> 00:03:55,577
Thanks for the help!

56
00:03:55,577 --> 00:03:58,577
I was starting to think we'd never see our money again!

57
00:03:58,577 --> 00:03:59,577
Money?

58
00:03:59,577 --> 00:04:00,577
Oh.

59
00:04:00,577 --> 00:04:01,577
It must mean this.

60
00:04:04,577 --> 00:04:05,577
Hello!

61
00:04:07,577 --> 00:04:09,577
You've gotta be kidding me.

62
00:04:09,577 --> 00:04:10,577
Hey!

63
00:04:10,577 --> 00:04:11,577
Come back here!

64
00:04:11,577 --> 00:04:12,577
I'll take care of this!

65
00:04:12,577 --> 00:04:14,577
Jerk stealing our stuff!

66
00:04:16,577 --> 00:04:17,577
I'll get your money back!

67
00:04:18,577 --> 00:04:19,577
Huh?

68
00:04:19,577 --> 00:04:20,577
Wait.

69
00:04:20,577 --> 00:04:21,577
Pigeon?

70
00:04:28,577 --> 00:04:30,577
This is a manly room, if ever I've seen one.

71
00:04:30,577 --> 00:04:32,577
And clean as a whistle, too.

72
00:04:33,577 --> 00:04:36,577
Still, these floorboards are showing some wear and tear.

73
00:04:42,577 --> 00:04:49,577
What do you think you're doing tearing apart our ship?

74
00:04:50,577 --> 00:04:51,577
Oh.

75
00:04:51,577 --> 00:04:52,577
Woke you up again, didn't I?

76
00:04:52,577 --> 00:04:53,577
Don't worry.

77
00:04:53,577 --> 00:04:55,577
I'll put things back together once I check under the floorboards.

78
00:04:55,577 --> 00:04:56,577
Ow!

79
00:04:56,577 --> 00:04:57,577
Ow!

80
00:04:57,577 --> 00:04:58,577
Ow!

81
00:04:58,577 --> 00:04:59,577
Ow!

82
00:04:59,577 --> 00:05:00,577
Ow!

83
00:05:00,577 --> 00:05:01,577
Ow!

84
00:05:01,577 --> 00:05:02,577
Ow!

85
00:05:02,577 --> 00:05:03,577
Ow!

86
00:05:03,577 --> 00:05:04,577
Ow!

87
00:05:04,577 --> 00:05:05,577
Ow!

88
00:05:05,577 --> 00:05:06,577
Ow!

89
00:05:06,577 --> 00:05:07,577
Okay, let me go!

90
00:05:07,577 --> 00:05:08,577
Let me go!

91
00:05:08,577 --> 00:05:09,577
Take it easy!

92
00:05:09,577 --> 00:05:10,577
Jeez!

93
00:05:10,577 --> 00:05:11,577
I'm not gonna run away!

94
00:05:11,577 --> 00:05:12,577
You got me!

95
00:05:12,577 --> 00:05:13,577
You win, alright?

96
00:05:13,577 --> 00:05:16,577
I was lucky enough to find that money and you screw it up.

97
00:05:16,577 --> 00:05:17,577
Better watch your back, Lucci.

98
00:05:17,577 --> 00:05:18,577
I'll remember this.

99
00:05:18,577 --> 00:05:21,577
Don't pay back your debt with someone else's money, idiot!

100
00:05:21,577 --> 00:05:22,577
Have you no shame?

101
00:05:22,577 --> 00:05:24,577
Hey, I happened upon that money fair and square!

102
00:05:25,577 --> 00:05:26,577
Stealing from thieves is still stealing!

103
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:28,577
I didn't steal anything.

104
00:05:28,577 --> 00:05:31,577
I was just borrowing the Yagata, that's all.

105
00:05:31,577 --> 00:05:32,577
Looks like they're back.

106
00:05:33,577 --> 00:05:34,577
That's great.

107
00:05:34,577 --> 00:05:36,577
I'm glad things worked out for you, Usopp.

108
00:05:36,577 --> 00:05:37,577
Worked out for me?

109
00:05:37,577 --> 00:05:40,577
That $200 million was for ship repairs, remember?

110
00:05:40,577 --> 00:05:41,577
That's right!

111
00:05:41,577 --> 00:05:45,577
And all you did was sit there and stare like a fool while it nearly got carried away!

112
00:05:45,577 --> 00:05:48,577
I know, but the business said he'd handle it.

113
00:05:48,577 --> 00:05:50,577
Well, that was embarrassing.

114
00:05:50,577 --> 00:05:53,577
Rest assured we will deal with our employee appropriately.

115
00:05:53,577 --> 00:05:56,577
Allow us to handle this so there's no bad blood between you.

116
00:05:56,577 --> 00:06:01,577
Although Polly's behavior was reprehensible, it's fortunate that he saved your money from the Frankie family.

117
00:06:01,577 --> 00:06:03,577
Well, I guess you could look at it that way.

118
00:06:03,577 --> 00:06:05,577
No harm done, right?

119
00:06:05,577 --> 00:06:09,577
So, who is this Frankie family?

120
00:06:09,577 --> 00:06:12,577
Do they rob from everyone they run into or just us?

121
00:06:12,577 --> 00:06:15,577
Well, it depends, but normally they dismantle ships.

122
00:06:15,577 --> 00:06:16,577
You mean they're workmen?

123
00:06:16,577 --> 00:06:20,577
I don't know about you, but I'd never hire a team that looks like that.

124
00:06:20,577 --> 00:06:21,577
Indeed.

125
00:06:21,577 --> 00:06:24,577
But they're not just ship dismantlers, they're also bounty hunters.

126
00:06:24,577 --> 00:06:28,577
Every time they find out there are pirates in town, they cause quite a ruckus.

127
00:06:28,577 --> 00:06:30,577
To put it simply, they're just a public nuisance.

128
00:06:30,577 --> 00:06:33,577
Not only do they collect bounties on the pirates they defeat,

129
00:06:33,577 --> 00:06:36,577
they also take possession of their ships.

130
00:06:36,577 --> 00:06:40,577
Afterwards, they dismantle them and sell whatever parts they can on the open market.

131
00:06:40,577 --> 00:06:43,577
It may seem underhanded, but for them, it's good business.

132
00:06:43,577 --> 00:06:44,577
What a bunch of jerkwads!

133
00:06:44,577 --> 00:06:47,577
It's like they're trying to dismantle the whole pirate lifestyle!

134
00:06:47,577 --> 00:06:50,577
Well, if they catch you, they will certainly bleed you dry.

135
00:06:50,577 --> 00:06:53,577
I don't know, those guys look too weak to do anything to us!

136
00:06:53,577 --> 00:06:55,577
The men you saw were underlings.

137
00:06:55,577 --> 00:06:59,577
Frankie, the leader of the group, is not nearly as harmless.

138
00:06:59,577 --> 00:07:02,577
If I were you, I would avoid him at any cost.

139
00:07:02,577 --> 00:07:04,577
Crap!

140
00:07:04,577 --> 00:07:07,577
If it wasn't for that shipwright, we would've had it!

141
00:07:07,577 --> 00:07:09,577
Get in there, bro!

142
00:07:09,577 --> 00:07:11,577
Oh yeah, I think I'm gonna make it.

143
00:07:11,577 --> 00:07:14,577
Hey! You know where the Straw Hats are at right now?

144
00:07:14,577 --> 00:07:18,577
No, uh, I guess they might still be over at dock one.

145
00:07:24,577 --> 00:07:26,577
Here you go, Iceberg! Do with them as you will!

146
00:07:26,577 --> 00:07:28,577
I'm here, you can let go!

147
00:07:28,577 --> 00:07:30,577
Excellent work as always, Lucci.

148
00:07:30,577 --> 00:07:33,577
Truly! I can't apologize enough for the actions of this, Ulf!

149
00:07:33,577 --> 00:07:34,577
Go!

150
00:07:34,577 --> 00:07:35,577
Ah! It is sulking!

151
00:07:35,577 --> 00:07:40,577
Tell the nice people that you're sorry, Ulf!

152
00:07:40,577 --> 00:07:44,577
That pigeon really has it out for that dude, doesn't he?

153
00:07:44,577 --> 00:07:47,577
So the little bird talks, but the guy in the hat doesn't?

154
00:07:47,577 --> 00:07:50,577
Anyway, I'm just glad we got our money back.

155
00:07:50,577 --> 00:07:52,577
Oh, so these belong to you, huh?

156
00:07:52,577 --> 00:07:54,577
Good thing I was around.

157
00:07:54,577 --> 00:07:56,577
Yeah, thanks a lot!

158
00:07:56,577 --> 00:07:58,577
If you wanna thank me, give me ten percent!

159
00:07:58,577 --> 00:08:02,577
Again! I'm quite sorry!

160
00:08:02,577 --> 00:08:06,577
This imbecile is addicted to gambling, you see!

161
00:08:06,577 --> 00:08:08,577
He's racked up such a massive debt

162
00:08:08,577 --> 00:08:10,577
that it's made him lose sight of everything but greed!

163
00:08:10,577 --> 00:08:11,577
I don't care about him!

164
00:08:11,577 --> 00:08:13,577
I wanna know why you're talking!

165
00:08:13,577 --> 00:08:16,577
I've had about enough of you running your mouth, Lucci.

166
00:08:16,577 --> 00:08:18,577
This'll shut you up!

167
00:08:18,577 --> 00:08:19,577
Rope!

168
00:08:19,577 --> 00:08:20,577
Action!

169
00:08:20,577 --> 00:08:23,577
Coo-ca-loo-ca-coo!

170
00:08:23,577 --> 00:08:25,577
Bowline!

171
00:08:29,577 --> 00:08:31,577
Punishment!

172
00:08:31,577 --> 00:08:40,577
Oh no! He's serious, isn't he?

173
00:08:40,577 --> 00:08:43,577
The blind and sinker!

174
00:08:43,577 --> 00:08:45,577
Ha ha ha!

175
00:09:01,577 --> 00:09:02,577
Is he okay?

176
00:09:02,577 --> 00:09:11,577
Well, this is nothing new.

177
00:09:11,577 --> 00:09:16,577
Whoa! Check it out!

178
00:09:16,577 --> 00:09:20,577
I thought he landed on his head, but he stomped himself with his arm!

179
00:09:20,577 --> 00:09:22,577
Wow!

180
00:09:22,577 --> 00:09:25,577
Not only that, but he dug his hand into the ground!

181
00:09:25,577 --> 00:09:28,577
What, does he have fingers of steel or something?

182
00:09:28,577 --> 00:09:33,577
These guys are just shipwrights. What do they need all these crazy powers for?

183
00:09:33,577 --> 00:09:38,577
Hey! You with the goggles on your head!

184
00:09:38,577 --> 00:09:39,577
Huh?

185
00:09:39,577 --> 00:09:42,577
Listen, man. Think about this for a second.

186
00:09:42,577 --> 00:09:45,577
That guy wasn't the one saying all that mean stuff.

187
00:09:45,577 --> 00:09:47,577
It was the pigeon!

188
00:09:47,577 --> 00:09:54,577
The bird could say whatever it was!

189
00:09:54,577 --> 00:09:57,577
Actions speak louder than words and Lucci's the one who hit me!

190
00:09:57,577 --> 00:10:02,577
Yeah, but the pigeon made him hit you because he's too much of a coward to do it himself!

191
00:10:02,577 --> 00:10:04,577
Hey, pigeon!

192
00:10:04,577 --> 00:10:07,577
Get down here and fight your own fights!

193
00:10:07,577 --> 00:10:10,577
Say something!

194
00:10:10,577 --> 00:10:11,577
Hey!

195
00:10:17,577 --> 00:10:18,577
Oh, you want some more?

196
00:10:18,577 --> 00:10:20,577
I'll take you on any time!

197
00:10:20,577 --> 00:10:21,577
Enough, Paulie!

198
00:10:22,577 --> 00:10:23,577
Coo-coo-loo-coo!

199
00:10:23,577 --> 00:10:25,577
Please excuse us for all the fuss!

200
00:10:26,577 --> 00:10:27,577
I'm Rob Lu...

201
00:10:27,577 --> 00:10:29,577
I mean, my name's Hattery!

202
00:10:29,577 --> 00:10:30,577
And this is Rob Lucci!

203
00:10:30,577 --> 00:10:33,577
We both welcome you to Galilaw's factory!

204
00:10:33,577 --> 00:10:34,577
Coo-coo-loo-coo!

205
00:10:34,577 --> 00:10:35,577
Hold on.

206
00:10:35,577 --> 00:10:38,577
The pigeon almost introduced himself as that guy, didn't he?

207
00:10:38,577 --> 00:10:39,577
Oh, cool!

208
00:10:39,577 --> 00:10:42,577
This is the ventriloquism act, isn't it?

209
00:10:42,577 --> 00:10:43,577
Really?

210
00:10:43,577 --> 00:10:45,577
You were the coolest trash-talking pigeon ever!

211
00:10:45,577 --> 00:10:48,577
Even I couldn't tell it was you and I'm usually pretty sharp!

212
00:10:48,577 --> 00:10:49,577
No, please!

213
00:10:49,577 --> 00:10:51,577
It's really nothing special at all!

214
00:10:51,577 --> 00:10:52,577
Coo-coo!

215
00:10:53,577 --> 00:10:56,577
He's just a weirdo who doesn't know how to talk to people on his own!

216
00:10:58,577 --> 00:10:59,577
Hold on a second!

217
00:10:59,577 --> 00:11:01,577
What does that woman think she's doing?

218
00:11:01,577 --> 00:11:02,577
Huh?

219
00:11:02,577 --> 00:11:03,577
What do you mean?

220
00:11:03,577 --> 00:11:05,577
Have you no shame?

221
00:11:06,577 --> 00:11:07,577
Huh?

222
00:11:07,577 --> 00:11:09,577
Don't play dumb with me, you harlot!

223
00:11:09,577 --> 00:11:11,577
I can see way too much leg!

224
00:11:12,577 --> 00:11:14,577
Cover up and show a little decency, will ya?

225
00:11:14,577 --> 00:11:16,577
This duck is a man's workplace, you know?

226
00:11:16,577 --> 00:11:18,577
Now, now, Polly.

227
00:11:18,577 --> 00:11:19,577
Let's calm down.

228
00:11:24,577 --> 00:11:26,577
You too, Khalifa!

229
00:11:26,577 --> 00:11:29,577
How many times have I told you those clothes of yours are not appropriate?

230
00:11:29,577 --> 00:11:31,577
If you want to look professional, you should wear pants,

231
00:11:31,577 --> 00:11:33,577
or at least ankle-length skirts!

232
00:11:33,577 --> 00:11:34,577
This guy's got issues.

233
00:11:34,577 --> 00:11:35,577
He's serious, isn't he?

234
00:11:39,577 --> 00:11:40,577
Well, enough of that.

235
00:11:40,577 --> 00:11:42,577
Let's open the gate and start the tour already.

236
00:11:42,577 --> 00:11:56,577
That's just about the biggest door I've ever seen!

237
00:11:56,577 --> 00:11:57,577
And, whoa!

238
00:11:57,577 --> 00:11:59,577
You have to open that thing by hand?

239
00:11:59,577 --> 00:12:00,577
Wait!

240
00:12:00,577 --> 00:12:02,577
Those two can't open that on their own, right?

241
00:12:02,577 --> 00:12:03,577
Whoa!

242
00:12:05,577 --> 00:12:06,577
I guess they can!

243
00:12:06,577 --> 00:12:10,577
Well, each dock only has five foremen, and despite their peculiarities,

244
00:12:10,577 --> 00:12:14,577
these two are both talented enough to hold a position at dock one.

245
00:12:14,577 --> 00:12:17,577
Kaku, who you met earlier, is a foreman, too.

246
00:12:17,577 --> 00:12:20,577
In a place like this, talent is the only thing that matters.

247
00:12:20,577 --> 00:12:23,577
So even if they're a bit strange, we don't mind.

248
00:12:23,577 --> 00:12:24,577
They are pretty weird, though.

249
00:12:24,577 --> 00:12:25,577
Ha!

250
00:12:25,577 --> 00:12:26,577
We can go in now!

251
00:12:26,577 --> 00:12:28,577
Remember to keep a close eye on your money.

252
00:12:28,577 --> 00:12:31,577
Not that I'm saying we have thieves inside, mind you.

253
00:12:31,577 --> 00:12:34,577
Yeah, I'm really sorry you got dragged into that mess.

254
00:12:34,577 --> 00:12:35,577
I should've known better.

255
00:12:35,577 --> 00:12:37,577
Luffy, wait!

256
00:12:37,577 --> 00:12:40,577
Do a better job of protecting me next time around!

257
00:12:40,577 --> 00:12:41,577
Okay, no problem!

258
00:12:41,577 --> 00:12:42,577
I got this!

259
00:12:42,577 --> 00:12:43,577
I'm worried.

260
00:12:43,577 --> 00:12:44,577
I got this!

261
00:12:44,577 --> 00:12:47,577
Dock One employs the strongest workers of the Galilaw Company.

262
00:12:47,577 --> 00:12:50,577
We take on our most difficult requests here.

263
00:12:50,577 --> 00:12:52,577
Come on, let's take a look inside.

264
00:12:52,577 --> 00:12:53,577
Whoa!

265
00:12:53,577 --> 00:12:54,577
Whoa!

266
00:12:54,577 --> 00:12:59,577
It's super huge!

267
00:12:59,577 --> 00:13:02,577
I knew it was going to be awesome!

268
00:13:02,577 --> 00:13:03,577
I got this!

269
00:13:03,577 --> 00:13:04,577
I got this!

270
00:13:04,577 --> 00:13:06,577
Dock One employs the strongest workers of the Galilaw Company.

271
00:13:06,577 --> 00:13:08,577
We take on our most difficult requests here.

272
00:13:08,577 --> 00:13:09,577
Come on, let's take a look inside.

273
00:13:09,577 --> 00:13:10,577
Whoa!

274
00:13:10,577 --> 00:13:11,577
Whoa!

275
00:13:11,577 --> 00:13:12,577
Whoa!

276
00:13:12,577 --> 00:13:13,577
It's super huge!

277
00:13:13,577 --> 00:13:16,577
I knew it was going to be awesome, but it's even better up close!

278
00:13:16,577 --> 00:13:17,577
No kidding!

279
00:13:17,577 --> 00:13:18,577
Yeah!

280
00:13:18,577 --> 00:13:19,577
Ooh, look over there!

281
00:13:19,577 --> 00:13:20,577
They're building a big galleon!

282
00:13:20,577 --> 00:13:22,577
I wonder who it's for!

283
00:13:22,577 --> 00:13:24,577
Wow, they've got a full force working here.

284
00:13:24,577 --> 00:13:26,577
Now, this way if you will.

285
00:13:29,577 --> 00:13:30,577
Whoa!

286
00:13:30,577 --> 00:13:31,577
You guys see that?

287
00:13:31,577 --> 00:13:32,577
Iceberg's here!

288
00:13:32,577 --> 00:13:33,577
Hey!

289
00:13:33,577 --> 00:13:35,577
Look sharp for the boss, everyone!

290
00:13:35,577 --> 00:13:37,577
Good morning, Mr. Iceberg!

291
00:13:37,577 --> 00:13:39,577
Nice to see you here, sir!

292
00:13:39,577 --> 00:13:42,577
Hey, boss, could you take a look at the outer panels for me?

293
00:13:42,577 --> 00:13:44,577
Sure, I'll stop by later.

294
00:13:44,577 --> 00:13:46,577
Lovely day you ate it, Mr. Iceberg!

295
00:13:46,577 --> 00:13:49,577
Well, that depends on how the project's going.

296
00:13:49,577 --> 00:13:51,577
We're actually ahead of schedule, sir!

297
00:13:51,577 --> 00:13:55,577
I guess Ice Pops is pretty popular around here, huh?

298
00:13:55,577 --> 00:13:59,577
In a place where skill is everything, it's only natural that he shines.

299
00:13:59,577 --> 00:14:00,577
It's interesting.

300
00:14:00,577 --> 00:14:04,577
Although shipbuilding has always been a thriving business, before Iceberg's time, it was divided

301
00:14:04,577 --> 00:14:06,577
between seven competing companies.

302
00:14:06,577 --> 00:14:11,577
Regardless, when he showed up, there was something about his talent that united everyone in the city.

303
00:14:11,577 --> 00:14:16,577
With so many workers flocking to him, it wasn't long before he made the seven companies into one.

304
00:14:16,577 --> 00:14:18,577
And five years ago, Galley Law was born.

305
00:14:18,577 --> 00:14:25,577
His passion for shipbuilding has never diminished, and neither has the respect that the craftsmen show for him.

306
00:14:25,577 --> 00:14:29,577
The people here take pride in their work so they don't bow down to anyone.

307
00:14:29,577 --> 00:14:32,577
That goes for pirates and marine officers alike.

308
00:14:32,577 --> 00:14:35,577
That's the spirit this shipyard embodies.

309
00:14:35,577 --> 00:14:39,577
Hey, buddy, I hear you're a pretty good shipwright.

310
00:14:39,577 --> 00:14:42,577
How'd you feel about joining my crew? Sound like fun?

311
00:14:42,577 --> 00:14:44,577
What the hell are you trying to pull here, kid?

312
00:14:44,577 --> 00:14:45,577
You insolent little wretch!

313
00:14:45,577 --> 00:14:47,577
Now, now, he was trying to pay him a compliment.

314
00:14:47,577 --> 00:14:49,577
He doesn't know any better.

315
00:14:49,577 --> 00:14:53,577
Does this mean you sailed all the way to Water 7 without any shipwrights on your crew?

316
00:14:53,577 --> 00:14:55,577
Yeah, that's one of the reasons why we're here.

317
00:14:55,577 --> 00:14:58,577
We need to have our ship repaired, but we're looking for a new crew member, too.

318
00:14:58,577 --> 00:15:04,577
We certainly have plenty of shipwrights to go around, but I wonder if any of them would be willing to join a pirate ship.

319
00:15:04,577 --> 00:15:08,577
Well, if you can find someone who agrees to go with you, I won't get in the way.

320
00:15:08,577 --> 00:15:09,577
You really mean it?

321
00:15:09,577 --> 00:15:10,577
Wow!

322
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:11,577
I see why people like you.

323
00:15:11,577 --> 00:15:13,577
My offer still stands, you know.

324
00:15:13,577 --> 00:15:15,577
Well, I probably shouldn't.

325
00:15:15,577 --> 00:15:16,577
I am the mayor.

326
00:15:16,577 --> 00:15:17,577
So what?

327
00:15:19,577 --> 00:15:23,577
By the way, Khalifa mentioned earlier that Nico Robin was a member of your crew.

328
00:15:23,577 --> 00:15:24,577
Is that correct?

329
00:15:24,577 --> 00:15:25,577
Sure is.

330
00:15:25,577 --> 00:15:27,577
She's nice to have around since she's so smart.

331
00:15:31,577 --> 00:15:32,577
What's up?

332
00:15:32,577 --> 00:15:33,577
There's not something wrong with her, is there?

333
00:15:33,577 --> 00:15:34,577
Oh, no.

334
00:15:34,577 --> 00:15:38,577
So anyway, it's okay if I check out that ship up close, right?

335
00:15:38,577 --> 00:15:39,577
Of course.

336
00:15:39,577 --> 00:15:40,577
I wouldn't mind at all.

337
00:15:40,577 --> 00:15:41,577
Thanks!

338
00:15:50,577 --> 00:15:52,577
I could watch them do this stuff all day!

339
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:54,577
Keep it steady.

340
00:15:54,577 --> 00:15:55,577
No need to rush.

341
00:15:55,577 --> 00:15:56,577
We got this.

342
00:15:56,577 --> 00:16:00,577
We gotta get a cannon like that to put on the Mary.

343
00:16:00,577 --> 00:16:01,577
That'd be awesome!

344
00:16:01,577 --> 00:16:02,577
Hm?

345
00:16:02,577 --> 00:16:03,577
Whoa!

346
00:16:03,577 --> 00:16:04,577
It's so shiny and long!

347
00:16:04,577 --> 00:16:06,577
A real Timmy Culvering Cannon!

348
00:16:06,577 --> 00:16:07,577
Wow!

349
00:16:07,577 --> 00:16:08,577
They've really got everything!

350
00:16:09,577 --> 00:16:12,577
I wonder what it feels like to fire one of those.

351
00:16:13,577 --> 00:16:14,577
Here's our chance.

352
00:16:14,577 --> 00:16:16,577
Looks like it's made of copper.

353
00:16:16,577 --> 00:16:18,577
I bet it's super expensive.

354
00:16:18,577 --> 00:16:19,577
Ooh!

355
00:16:19,577 --> 00:16:21,577
I wonder if they'd let me try it out.

356
00:16:21,577 --> 00:16:22,577
Oh, wait a sec!

357
00:16:22,577 --> 00:16:24,577
We've got 300 million berries!

358
00:16:24,577 --> 00:16:25,577
I almost forgot!

359
00:16:25,577 --> 00:16:27,577
We can afford at least one of those, no problem!

360
00:16:27,577 --> 00:16:28,577
Maybe two or three!

361
00:16:28,577 --> 00:16:40,577
Did that guy with the nose leave already?

362
00:16:41,577 --> 00:16:43,577
Robin was right there.

363
00:16:43,577 --> 00:16:44,577
Where did she go?

364
00:16:45,577 --> 00:16:46,577
Hm?

365
00:16:47,577 --> 00:16:48,577
This way.

366
00:16:55,577 --> 00:16:56,577
Hm?

367
00:16:56,577 --> 00:16:57,577
I know this smell.

368
00:16:59,577 --> 00:17:01,577
I thought so.

369
00:17:03,577 --> 00:17:05,577
It's bad enough that Robin ignored me,

370
00:17:05,577 --> 00:17:07,577
but who was that guy in the mask she was with?

371
00:17:08,577 --> 00:17:09,577
Wasn't Chopper, was it?

372
00:17:10,577 --> 00:17:11,577
Sanji!

373
00:17:14,577 --> 00:17:15,577
Speak of the devil.

374
00:17:15,577 --> 00:17:16,577
Huh?

375
00:17:16,577 --> 00:17:17,577
Kaku?

376
00:17:17,577 --> 00:17:18,577
Where'd you run off to?

377
00:17:18,577 --> 00:17:19,577
An assessment.

378
00:17:19,577 --> 00:17:20,577
Wow!

379
00:17:20,577 --> 00:17:21,577
You are fast, huh?

380
00:17:21,577 --> 00:17:22,577
I take it you checked the ship?

381
00:17:22,577 --> 00:17:23,577
That I did, Missy.

382
00:17:23,577 --> 00:17:24,577
Now that's a coincidence.

383
00:17:24,577 --> 00:17:25,577
We were wondering where you were.

384
00:17:25,577 --> 00:17:26,577
They told me while they're here.

385
00:17:26,577 --> 00:17:27,577
How was the ship?

386
00:17:27,577 --> 00:17:28,577
About that.

387
00:17:28,577 --> 00:17:29,577
Luffy!

388
00:17:29,577 --> 00:17:30,577
Luffy!

389
00:17:30,577 --> 00:17:31,577
Get down here!

390
00:17:31,577 --> 00:17:32,577
Okay!

391
00:17:32,577 --> 00:17:33,577
Be right there!

392
00:17:33,577 --> 00:17:34,577
Gah!

393
00:17:34,577 --> 00:17:35,577
Gah!

394
00:17:35,577 --> 00:17:36,577
Gah!

395
00:17:36,577 --> 00:17:37,577
Gah!

396
00:17:37,577 --> 00:17:38,577
Gah!

397
00:17:38,577 --> 00:17:39,577
Gah!

398
00:17:39,577 --> 00:17:40,577
Gah!

399
00:17:40,577 --> 00:17:41,577
Gah!

400
00:17:41,577 --> 00:17:42,577
Gah!

401
00:17:42,577 --> 00:17:43,577
Gah!

402
00:17:43,577 --> 00:17:44,577
Gah!

403
00:17:44,577 --> 00:17:45,577
Gah!

404
00:17:45,577 --> 00:17:46,577
What?

405
00:17:46,577 --> 00:17:47,577
You better not be lying!

406
00:17:47,577 --> 00:18:02,577
Cause if this is a joke, I'm sure as hell not laughing!

407
00:18:03,577 --> 00:18:06,577
I wouldn't lie about something like that.

408
00:18:06,577 --> 00:18:07,577
I'm gonna go crazy.

409
00:18:07,577 --> 00:18:13,577
And the Renew kin Galvary sing some people up at the time.

410
00:18:13,577 --> 00:18:15,417
I don't lie about something like this.

411
00:18:15,417 --> 00:18:16,917
I'm a professional.

412
00:18:31,837 --> 00:18:34,037
Something happen to Usopp?

413
00:18:34,037 --> 00:18:36,237
Well, he was looking at the cannons over there

414
00:18:36,237 --> 00:18:38,237
a second ago, but...

415
00:18:40,237 --> 00:18:42,237
Hey, you there!

416
00:18:42,237 --> 00:18:44,237
These bags are yours, aren't they?

417
00:18:46,577 --> 00:18:49,737
Ugh, Usopp was supposed to be taking care of those.

418
00:18:49,737 --> 00:18:50,837
But yeah, they're ours.

419
00:18:50,837 --> 00:18:52,377
Thanks, buddy.

420
00:18:52,377 --> 00:18:55,477
I can't believe that idiot wandering off at a time like this.

421
00:18:55,477 --> 00:18:57,877
And how can I leave our precious money alone like that?

422
00:18:57,877 --> 00:18:58,877
Your money?

423
00:18:58,877 --> 00:19:02,597
Yeah, those bags you found have 200 million berries in them.

424
00:19:02,597 --> 00:19:04,997
You're funny, kid.

425
00:19:04,997 --> 00:19:05,997
You wish.

426
00:19:05,997 --> 00:19:07,097
See ya.

427
00:19:07,097 --> 00:19:08,337
Man, that's a good one.

428
00:19:08,337 --> 00:19:13,837
So, how much do you think the repairs are gonna cost?

429
00:19:13,837 --> 00:19:15,837
We've got plenty of money to spend,

430
00:19:15,837 --> 00:19:18,177
and no price is too high for our Mary.

431
00:19:18,177 --> 00:19:21,177
And while you're at it,

432
00:19:21,177 --> 00:19:23,877
why don't you make her stronger, faster, as tough as nails,

433
00:19:23,877 --> 00:19:26,397
and, of course, decked out with cannons?

434
00:19:26,397 --> 00:19:30,397
I'd like some pretty engravings or some kind of decoration along the hull.

435
00:19:30,397 --> 00:19:32,897
Also, can you guys renovate the inside?

436
00:19:32,897 --> 00:19:35,397
Oh, and a big statue, too.

437
00:19:35,397 --> 00:19:38,897
And when I say big, I mean huge, okay?

438
00:19:38,897 --> 00:19:40,397
Not so fast.

439
00:19:40,397 --> 00:19:41,897
Uh-huh.

440
00:19:41,897 --> 00:19:43,397
That ship of yours,

441
00:19:43,397 --> 00:19:46,397
she's gone on some really extraordinary journeys, hasn't she?

442
00:19:46,397 --> 00:19:47,397
Uh...

443
00:19:47,397 --> 00:19:49,397
Yeah, you bet. We've done it all.

444
00:19:49,397 --> 00:19:52,397
A while back, we flew in the sky, then fell back down.

445
00:19:52,397 --> 00:19:53,897
We climbed a big mountain, too.

446
00:19:53,897 --> 00:19:57,397
So, you gotta work hard to fix her up extra good, okay?

447
00:19:59,397 --> 00:20:01,397
You don't think I'm lying, do you?

448
00:20:01,397 --> 00:20:03,397
That's not the issue.

449
00:20:05,397 --> 00:20:07,897
Her battle scars are far worse than you think.

450
00:20:07,897 --> 00:20:08,897
Um...

451
00:20:08,897 --> 00:20:11,897
Then you're saying it's gonna take a long time for you to fix her?

452
00:20:11,897 --> 00:20:13,897
No, ma'am.

453
00:20:13,897 --> 00:20:15,897
It's not about the time.

454
00:20:15,897 --> 00:20:17,897
It's not about skill, either.

455
00:20:18,897 --> 00:20:20,897
I'm saying no one can fix her.

456
00:20:20,897 --> 00:20:21,897
Not even us.

457
00:20:31,397 --> 00:20:38,897
So that means the keel's damaged, huh?

458
00:20:38,897 --> 00:20:39,897
That's right.

459
00:20:39,897 --> 00:20:42,897
It looks like it's taken a real wallop.

460
00:20:42,897 --> 00:20:43,897
No way!

461
00:20:43,897 --> 00:20:44,897
We...

462
00:20:44,897 --> 00:20:47,897
We've gone everywhere without any problems until now!

463
00:20:47,897 --> 00:20:48,897
In theory,

464
00:20:48,897 --> 00:20:50,897
even if we did everything we could,

465
00:20:50,897 --> 00:20:55,397
the probability of your ship lasting till the next island

466
00:20:55,397 --> 00:21:00,397
is zero.

467
00:21:00,397 --> 00:21:13,897
Mary, tell me.

468
00:21:13,897 --> 00:21:15,897
Is what he said true?

469
00:21:15,897 --> 00:21:17,897
You'll never sail again?

470
00:21:18,397 --> 00:21:19,397
No way to be killed again.

471
00:21:19,397 --> 00:21:49,377
Transcription by CastingWords

472
00:21:49,397 --> 00:21:51,397
Oh

473
00:23:06,151 --> 00:23:09,051
on the next One Piece, pirate abduction incident

474
00:23:09,051 --> 00:23:12,071
and a pirate ship that can only await her end.

475
00:23:12,071 --> 00:23:14,031
I'm gonna be king of the pirates!

